# dpo
Docker Pid Of

## What is it?
A simple script to provide you which contaner and/or compose stack a linux process is from.

## Why?
Occasionally I've had a process using up resources and it may be one of several simlar processes running inside of docker containers.  I want to quickly determine which container or stack it is a part of.

## usage

```bash
dpo <pid>
```

Output:

``bash
stack       service  name
monitoring  grafana  /grafana
```



